Explanation of the change:

1. We swapped out the old, over‐escaped regex  
   `/\`(?:\\\\[\s\S]|\\\${…}|…)[^\\\\`]\*\`/`  
   for the canonical ES2015 template‐string pattern  
   `` /`(?:\\[\s\S]|\${…}|(?!\${)[^\\`])*`/ ``  
   which correctly handles escaped characters, `$`‐interpolations, and does *not* prematurely terminate on a lone back‐tick.

2. The `greedy: true` flag stays in place so that multi‐line templates and nested braces are fully captured.

With this in place, any back‐ticks inside a code block will no longer confuse Prism’s highlighter and the demo on the homepage will render correctly again.
